      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Certainly, I'll clarify that for you. When individuals with transit visas undergo immigration control, stress is kept at a minimum to expedite the process. That said, the handwritten visa and I-TAD slip—the approved Travel Advisory for Asia—must be presented for verification. Common mistakes that can lead to immediate denial include damaged or unreadable documents, outdated I-TAD slips or visas, incorrect destination details on the visa, and missing among the documents any crucial paperwork like a valid return ticket. Officers are trained to meticulously check these details as they can quickly flag security or safety issues. It’s a crucial step to put all the documents in chronological order, circle the relevant I-TAD on the visa as per guidelines, make sure all notes and printing appear genuine and not forged, and verify that the return tickets are valid for a minimal duration of return flights. This ensures that officers have no ambiguity and the travel documents reflect a subsequent legitimate journey, which is the essence of a valid transit visa.",
